We aim to enhance the accuracy of structured text recognition by incorporating predefined formats defined through regular expressions, thereby facilitating the identification of specific patterns. Our method, involving a Weighted Finite-State Transducer model, boosts recognition accuracy on targeted formats, with minimal losses in other instances. A key parameter governs the intensity of the formatting influence. The proposed technique finds applications in text analysis, particularly when dealing with formatted documents, domain-specific lexicons, or known formats like driver's license numbers and medicinal prescription terminology. We evaluate the effectiveness of this approach on a range of structured text datasets and examine its implications on overall recognition performance. Additionally, we showcase its utility in various practical scenarios. Further details are available on our project website at the given link. \\

